course: dictionary
lesson: 3508
title: Fat: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word fat has more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find the right one. These words are its context, and they leave clues. «Penguins also keep warm with a thick layer of fat and tightly packed waterproof feathers.» Here fat is the soft layer under the skin that keeps an animal warm.
explain: Fat can also be a describing word. «A fat book» means a book that is thick or wide, not a book that is round and heavy in the body. Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Bears can live on their fat when they cannot find food. Their stored fat gives them energy through the winter. Fat is needed by the body, but too much of some kinds is unhealthy, so health lessons teach us to choose carefully.
explain: Calling a person fat is hurtful, because people come in all shapes and sizes. In a story, a fat cat or a fat raindrop is just a description of how something looks, and a dictionary can help when you are unsure.
fact: Fat is a natural oily substance found in foods like butter, oil, cheese and meat.
fact: Fat is also the soft layer under the skin of people and animals that stores energy and keeps them warm.
fact: As an adjective, «fat» means having a big, round body or a lot of fat, and it can change to fatter and fattest.
fact: «Fat» can mean thick or wide, as in «a fat book».
fact: «Fat chance» is an informal way to say no chance at all.
exercise: «Penguins keep warm with a thick layer of fat.» In this sentence, fat means | *A soft layer under the skin that keeps you warm | Tiny and light | A loud, noisy sound | A type of tasty cheese
exercise: «She carried a fat book home from the library.» Here fat means | A book about animals | A book that is very old and torn | *A book that is thick or wide | A book that is round and sticky
exercise: Which fact about fat is true? | Fat is only found in sweets and cakes | Fat is a kind of colour | Fat stops animals from feeling warm | *Fat is an oily substance found in foods like butter, oil and cheese
test:  Ben says, «Calling someone fat is a good joke.» Why is this a poor choice? | It means they are very tall | It is a kind compliment | It is funny to everyone | *It is hurtful, because people come in all shapes and sizes
test:  Which word is the adjective form that means having the biggest, roundest body? | fatly | fats | *fattest | fatter
exam:  «Fat chance» means | *No chance at all | A fat cat in a stripy hat | A very big chance | A chance to eat more cheese
